 1929; controlled by Marshal Tito as a communist state until his death in 1980","dna16":"8800153261000220","ex":["Tito's Yugoslavia included Slovenia, Croatia, Macedonia, Bosnia-Herzegovina, Serbia, and Montenegro"],"id":"oewn-yugoslavia__1.15.01..","pos":"noun","src":"wn","sym":"4:1","syn":[]},{"def":"A former country in Southeastern Europe in the Balkans, now split into 6 countries: Bosnia and Herzegovina, Croatia, North Macedonia, Montenegro, Serbia, and Slovenia.","dna16":"8800153261000329","ex":[],"id":"wikt:Yugoslavia:proper noun:3","pos":"proper noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":["South Slavia"],"tags":["historical"]},{"def":"The Kingdom of Yugoslavia, a kingdom ruled by the House of Karađorđević which existed from 1918 to 1941.","dna16":"8800153261000428","ex":[],"id":"wikt:Yugoslavia:proper noun:4","pos":"proper noun","src":"wikt","sym":"12:1","syn":["South Slavia"],"tags":["historical","specific"]},{"def":"The Federal People's Republic of Yugoslavia and the Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, a communist state which existed from 1945 to 1992.","dna16":"8800153261000527","ex":[],"id":"wikt:Yugoslavia:proper noun:5","pos":"proper noun","src":"wikt","sym":"0:1,12:1","syn":["South Slavia"],"tags":["historical","specific"]},{"def":"A former country in Southeastern Europe, a rump state formed by Serbia and Montenegro after 1992; in full, Federal Republic of Yugoslavia.","dna16":"8800153261000626","ex":[],"id":"wikt:Yugoslavia:proper noun:6","pos":"proper noun","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1,84:1","syn":["South Slavia"],"tags":["historical"]},{"def":"Serbia and Montenegro, after 2003 until 2006, when it disintegrated.","dna16":"8800153261000725","ex":[],"id":"wikt:Yugoslavia:proper noun:7","pos":"proper noun","src":"wikt","sym":"4:3","syn":["South Slavia"],"tags":["broadly","historical","nonstandard"]}]},"Yugoslavian":{"dna16":"8800153262000013","senses":[{"def":"of or relating to or characteristic of the former country of Yugoslavia or its people or languages","d